+# Local modification notice — 2026-10-17
+
+Based on ButterscotchRunner/Butterscotch revision `f6f1d30a2f933e5e0e77941251c7bd38e361a2ce`.
+
+`src/backends/web.c` adds a character event type, an `onCharacter(unsigned int)` entry point, and delivery to the existing `RunnerKeyboard_onCharacter` implementation through the frame input queue. This restores browser text entry through `keyboard_lastchar` and `keyboard_string`.
+
+The same backend adds synchronous read-only `agentSnapshot`, explicit pause setters/getters using the existing runner pause API, and an optional per-presented-frame JavaScript observer. `src/gl/gl_renderer.c` records game text draw calls for that observer, including placement, font, colors, alpha, and surface context; this captures text before a Draw event changes or destroys its writer. Collection is disabled unless a JavaScript `onAgentFrame` callback is installed. Each frame includes an explicit dropped-draw count if the 4096-call limit is reached. `src/runner.c` adds the existing pause flag to the JSON snapshot. `CMakeLists.txt` exports the added functions. No collision or gameplay rules were changed.
+
+Built on Windows with Emscripten 6.0.12, CMake 4.4.4, Ninja 1.13.2, and Emscripten SDK Python 3.13.3 / Node 24.19.0:
+
+```sh
+emcmake cmake -B build -G Ninja -DPLATFORM=web -DBACKEND=web -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION=ON
+cmake --build build --parallel 8
+```
+
+The complete upstream source and dependency license notices remain in this archive. See LICENSE for GNU AGPL v3 terms.
